      "structuredContent": {
        "url": "https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/hepta-private-ci/pull/5800",
        "number": 5800,
        "state": "open",
        "merged": false,
        "mergeable": false,
        "draft": true,
        "body": "The previous development runner could lose non-tensor PLIF dynamics when rebuilding a checkpoint, selected checkpoints only after a plateau-sized improvement, and averaged batch-normalized training losses by event count.\n\nThis stage serializes the complete PLIF configuration and selected spike-trace readout, saves every strict development improvement, separates the plateau anchor, aggregates weighted CE by target weight, records complete-epoch optimizer/RNG state, and supports an explicit ordered fit roster with process cost curves.\n\nValidation: all 13 core tests passed on the frozen v8 source and the canonical formatting-equivalent source. The actual 42-fit source archive is SHA256 288283cae2b2cf4e7b68432e040e643a5e1b00a7de961fc848dd5cf20eb46102. Results are development-only; final training adequacy, numerical scope and scientific benefit remain unconfirmed. The original 15,000-second global deadline can shorten later fits' actual nominal four-hour limits and must remain visible in costs.\n\nPublished through the connected API while the native control channel is unavailable. The entire tree equals local commit 6d18f16050dabab063a324087a7b4e00618bd1bb. The uncertain native publisher is left intact; this separate branch does not overwrite it or main.",
        "title": "HCSN: bind PLIF dynamics and record strict-best development training",
