        "draft": true,
        "body": "A capped fit must not be resumed from a partial or changed checkpoint, and a tensor-only state dictionary does not bind all model dynamics.\n\nThis stage adds fail-closed verification of the original completed epoch-cap result, outer process receipt, plan, initial/best/last checkpoints, event log, source and data identity. It independently reconstructs the complete model configuration from the original plan and recovers strict-best and plateau-anchor state.\n\nValidated as part of the frozen C1 delivery capsule: 24 tests passed (the existing 13 core tests plus 11 continuation tests), with the complete source unchanged. Capsule SHA256 f4b473aa4f373c1622bbdac90d61e33c64f0e9642b6c0506e7fec5b8885a3946. The continuation fixtures are synthetic; this does not establish scientific training or numerical-domain admission.\n\nThis is the first continuation stage and is stacked on the adequate-runner draft. Full tree identity equals local commit 372ecd8a8996abbae738850941c9789a7d3070aa.",
